            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Some are good value and some are modest machines suited to walking. Many are retailer-specific variants of mainstream models, so judge each one on its specifications — continuous horsepower, deck size, maximum user weight and warranty — compared with the nearest mainstream model from the same manufacturer, rather than on the brand or the store.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "What is Costco's return policy on treadmills?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Costco's return policy is widely regarded as generous, but terms can differ for some categories and for large or delivered items, and policies change. Check the current return terms on the product page or at the warehouse before buying, and find out how a return would work in practice for a heavy machine.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Does Costco deliver and assemble treadmills?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "It depends on the channel. Warehouse purchases are usually taken home by the member. Online listings for large items often include delivery in the price, but the level of delivery varies, and assembly may not be included or offered. Read the delivery terms on the listing and plan for assembly if it is not included.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Why can't I find the Costco treadmill model anywhere else?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Because many treadmills sold through large retailers are retailer-specific variants with their own model numbers. They are usually close to a mainstream model from the same manufacturer, but can differ in console, accessories, warranty or specifications. Compare specifications line by line, and ask the manufacturer what the model is based on.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Is it cheaper to buy a treadmill at Costco?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Sometimes. Prices on its selected models are often competitive and online prices frequently include delivery. Compare the delivered price against an equivalent specification elsewhere, include the membership fee if you are joining only for this, and weigh the return terms and warranty alongside the price.",
          },
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      headline: title,
      description: description,
      author: { "@type": "Person", name: "Morgan Reyes" },
      datePublished: "2026-10-06",
      dateModified: "2026-10-06",
      publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Treadmill Reviews USA" },
